<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Blazer-2.0.jpg" alt="A sketch portrait of a gray horse" width="400" height="521" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Blazer. 18"x14", oil on linen mounted on board. 2013.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This portrait sketch of Blazer is one of the holiday commissions that I completed this year. &nbsp;I managed to get some nice photographs of Blazer at the stable and the early December light was perfect for his light coat. &nbsp;The background for the painting was originally envisaged as a raw umber color, but after trying it out I decided to use an extension of the colors in his shadow side instead.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I painted in the portrait using just three colors: viridian, bright red and cadmium yellow light, plus burnt sienna for the halter and darker areas.</p>